---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { pipeSchedule40References as sizes, pipeLabel } from '../../data/pipe';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Pipe Size Reference — DN, NPS, A, OD & Wall | HowNote"
  description="Review HowNote's first cross-checked pipe-size subset with nominal DN, NPS and A labels separated from actual OD and wall thickness."
>
  <section class="hero container">
    <div class="eyebrow">HowNote Sizes · Pipe / Tube</div>
    <h1>Nominal size is not actual diameter.</h1>
    <p>HowNote keeps DN, NPS and regional A aliases separate from actual OD, wall thickness and calculated ID. The first public dataset is a deliberately limited Schedule 40 subset.</p>
    <div class="button-row">
      <a class="button" href="/tools/dn-nps-a-converter">Open size converter</a>
      <a class="button button-secondary" href="/tools/pipe-weight-calculator">Calculate pipe weight</a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="container related-section">
    <div class="card">
      <h2>Initial verified reference subset</h2>
      <p class="muted">The standard identity is sourced from ASME. The limited dimensions and nominal mass values are cross-checked against manufacturer publications. A labels are displayed only as regional convenience aliases.</p>
      <div class="table-wrap">
        <table>
          <thead>
            <tr><th>Nominal reference</th><th>OD mm</th><th>Wall mm</th><th>Calculated ID mm</th><th>Published kg/m</th><th></th></tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            {sizes.map((row, i) => {
              const insideDiameter = row.odMm - 2 * row.wallMm;
              return <tr>
                <td>{pipeLabel(row)}</td>
                <td>{row.odMm}</td>
                <td>{row.wallMm}</td>
                <td>{insideDiameter.toFixed(2)}</td>
                <td>{row.publishedKgM}</td>
                <td><a class="text-link" href={`/tools/pipe-weight-calculator?size=${i}`}>Calculate →</a></td>
              </tr>;
            })}
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="container grid">
    <article class="card">
      <div class="eyebrow">Nominal system</div>
      <h2>DN</h2>
      <p class="muted">DN is a dimensionless nominal designation. It is not a direct millimeter measurement of OD or ID.</p>
    </article>
    <article class="card">
      <div class="eyebrow">Nominal system</div>
      <h2>NPS</h2>
      <p class="muted">NPS is a nominal pipe size designation. Converting the NPS number directly to millimeters does not produce the actual OD.</p>
    </article>
    <article class="card">
      <div class="eyebrow">Regional alias</div>
      <h2>A designation</h2>
      <p class="muted">A labels such as 50A are shown for regional convenience and are kept separate from official ASME terminology.</p>
    </article>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
